  <div class="fs-faq-grid">
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>1. What is a fixed sidelight sliding door system?</h3>
    <p>A fixed sidelight sliding door system combines stationary glazed side panels with one or two active automatic sliding panels. The side panels remain stationary while the active doors move to provide entrance access.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>2. What configurations are available?</h3>
    <p>The OA300-SL is listed in three configurations: O-SX single-slide left hand, SX-O single-slide right hand and O-SX-SX-O bi-part.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>3. What is the difference between single-slide and bi-part?</h3>
    <p>A single-slide system uses one active sliding panel. A bi-part system uses two active panels that move apart from the centre to create the opening.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>4. What does O-SX mean?</h3>
    <p>O-SX is the brochure's code for the fixed sidelight left-hand arrangement. Confirm the final panel layout and handing with the approved project drawing.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>5. What does SX-O mean?</h3>
    <p>SX-O is the brochure's code for the fixed sidelight right-hand arrangement. The final handing should be checked against the approved shop drawing before fabrication.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>6. What does the bi-part configuration include?</h3>
    <p>The O-SX-SX-O configuration includes fixed sidelights at the outer sides and two active sliding panels that create a centre opening.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>7. What finishes are available?</h3>
    <p>The published finish options are Anodized Clear, listed as the standard finish, and Anodized Black, listed as the luxury finish.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>8. What motor is used in the OA300-SL?</h3>
    <p>The OA300-SL technical information specifies a 1/5 HP brushless DC motor with an enclosed hypoid gear drive.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>9. What is the maximum door panel weight?</h3>
    <p>The published OA300-SL specification lists a maximum door weight of up to 400 lbs per panel. Confirm the proposed door assembly and project details with Omega.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>10. What power supply does the system require?</h3>
    <p>The shared product specifications list a 120 VAC, 60 Hz power supply. Project electrical requirements should be confirmed during coordination.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>11. Can the opening and closing speed be adjusted?</h3>
    <p>Yes. The OA300-SL product information describes adjustable opening and closing speeds and forces, along with programmable opening-time settings.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="fs-faq">
    <h3>12. Does the system support manual operation?</h3>
